{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Edge Loops and Rings.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Edge Loops and Rings.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender edge loops and rings blender edge loops and rings","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Edge Loops and Rings.md","fileName":"Blender Edge Loops and Rings.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Edge Loops and Rings","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-07 23:25\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Mesh Modeling and Modifiers]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Mesh Modeling and Modifiers","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Edge Loops and Rings.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Edge Loops and Rings.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender edge loops and rings blender edge loops and rings","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Edge Loops and Rings.md","fileName":"Blender Edge Loops and Rings.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Edge Loops and Rings","heading":"Blender Edge Loops and Rings","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An edge loop follows a connected path through mesh topology. A closed loop returns to its beginning, while a terminating loop stops at a pole or another interruption in the surrounding edge flow.\n\nLoops make coherent surface regions easier to select and refine. Edge rings cross the mesh in the complementary direction, and loop cuts can introduce new rings whose position can be slid while preserving the broader form.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Mesh Modeling and Modifiers","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Edge Loops and Rings.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Edge Loops and Rings.md